course: dictionary
lesson: 10432
title: Tropical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tropical describes places near the equator, the hot middle of the Earth. These places are hot all year round, so the word tells you about heat as well as place.
explain: «Real sailors did bring parrots home from tropical voyages.» A voyage is a long journey, often by sea. The sailors went to warm, faraway places near the equator, so tropical must mean hot places near the middle of the Earth.
explain: Tropical also describes things from those places, like «tropical fish» and «tropical fruit». Ask yourself: where could this come from? A warm place near the equator. The sentence «bananas from a warm tropical farm» has a clue too: warm.
fact: Tropical means from or about places near the equator, the hot middle of the Earth.
fact: Tropical describes things from those places, like mangoes, pineapples and parrots.
fact: Tropical weather is hot and humid, which means hot and damp.
fact: «Mangroves grow with their feet in salty water along warm tropical coasts.»
fact: The Pantanal in Brazil is the world's biggest tropical wetland, a place where the land is often covered with water.
exercise: What does tropical mean in «tropical voyages»? | Voyages that were very short | Voyages to icy seas | *Voyages to hot places near the equator | Voyages in very small boats
exercise: «A bowl of breakfast can come from all over the world: bananas from a warm tropical farm.» Which word is a clue that a tropical farm is hot? | farm | *warm | bowl | breakfast
exercise: «Tropical weather is hot and humid.» What does humid mean? | Very loud | Dusty and dry | Freezing cold | *Damp, with lots of water in the air
test: «Mangroves grow with their feet in salty water along warm tropical coasts.» Where do mangroves grow? | In deserts far from the sea | *Along warm coasts near the equator | In snowy mountains | Deep under the ice
test: Which of these is most likely to be a tropical fruit? | Potato | Cabbage | Apple | *Pineapple
exam: «Tropical storms form over warm seas.» Where do tropical storms form? | On top of high mountains | Inside a desert | Over the frozen Arctic | *Over warm seas
